Multi-client (shared session) tests for tmux / xtmux.  Needs: Xvfb, openbox, wmctrl, xdotool, xwd +
ImageMagick (convert), python3 with pillow and pyte.  Run as root, or with a writable /run/utmux.
Build tmux/ and xtmux/ first (defaults: tmux/tmux and xtmux/xtmux in the repo; or set TMUX_BIN, XTMUX_BIN).

  python3 xtmux/tests/multiclient/mc_all.py [group ...]       (default: all groups)

Groups:
  keys             special keys (arrows...) typed in an observer arrive intact, xtmux and plain
  shrink           attaching from a smaller screen keeps short output visible; full screens crop the top
  pp               plain<->plain regression (attach takeover, mirroring, promotion, 3rd client)
  px               plain main, xtmux attaches (and xtmux detaching)
  xx               xtmux main, xtmux attaches: input and mirroring both ways
  detach_pair      main xtmux detaches -> observer promoted
  detach_lone      lone xtmux detaches -> daemon, window gone, re-attach works
  close            window-manager close: lone, and with a plain observer
  xloss            X server killed: lone, and with a plain observer
  obs_close        closing the observer's window ends only that client
  plainobs_detach  plain observer detaches; xtmux main unaffected
  race             8x detach -> attach (the attach-to-daemon race)
Each check prints PASS/FAIL; a summary follows.  mc_lib.py holds the helpers: plain tmux in a pty with a
pyte terminal emulator, and xtmux launched with its stdio on a pty, like from a terminal.
